      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_ynjcCq": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<strong>Why Cats Love Tunnels</strong>",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_faVBT6": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Cats in the wild hunt by stalking and hiding. Indoors, tunnels recreate that environment:</p><ul><li><br/><strong>Safe retreat</strong> – perfect for shy or anxious cats who need their own nook.<br/></li><li><br/><strong>Playground</strong> – encourages chasing, hide-and-seek, and ambush games.<br/></li><li><br/><strong>Exercise outlet</strong> – supports zoomies and weight control in a fun way.<br/></li><li><br/><strong>Multi-cat harmony</strong> – gives cats an outlet for play that reduces tension.<br/></li></ul><p>In my years of working with cats, tunnels have always been the one toy that never loses its novelty. Even senior cats who ignore most toys still perk up at the crinkle sound of a tunnel.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_ynjcCq",
        "text_faVBT6"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.rich-text.presets.name",
      "settings": {
        "desktop_content_position": "center",
        "content_alignment": "center",
