            "text": "<p><strong>Rescue cat confidence</strong>: A shy foster I cared for used the tunnel as a stepping stone toward engaging with people. She felt safe enough to peek out but still had privacy.</p><p><strong>Overweight cat success</strong>: A tunnel combined with toys turned lazy lounging into daily cardio, helping trim pounds without stress.<br/><br/><strong>Multi-cat play</strong>: Two brothers I worked with turned their tunnel into a racetrack. The peek windows kept them from colliding, and they played longer without fighting.</p>"
